00 <br>Demographic decline of Rome. c500,000 in 400 CE, less than 50,000 after the Gothic war (535-554 CE).<br>Rome’s population "might have been down to 300,000 in the late 4th century and down to 100,000 by 500, but it was still by far the largest city in Italy."<br>Under Theoderic the population of Ravenna "perhaps as large as 10,000. Naples, too, may have had a population as large as 10,000 at this time."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2952, 'temperature': 0.2})
